The meta backend (--split-mode tensor) copies a weight split along axis 0
(attn_output, ffn_down, ffn_down_exps: part of every row on each device) by
gathering each device's rows into a host buffer and copying it whole, in pieces
of 64 MiB, instead of one 2D copy from pageable memory. On LUMI-G's MI250X,
loads split as tensor ran at 100-230 MB/s, 10-50 times slower than split by
layer (Qwen3-235B Q4_K_M over four GCDs 943-1269 s against 19-145 s, the 480B
over eight 1679 s against 113, c11-placement, 18-19-10-2026), slower the more
GPUs, as if each of the hundreds of thousands of rows an expert tensor has per
device were copied on its own. GGML_META_GATHER_ROWS=0 restores the 2D copy.

